<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => this.size() == c.size();</code>

However, to ensure that the assertion correctly handles the case when the collection `c` is empty, we should adjust it to:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size();</code>

This assertion directly checks that the size of the newly constructed `HashSet` is equal to the size of the input collection `c`, which covers both non-empty and empty collections.
